{"parentUuid":"429e203b-5117-43e4-ac1e-940678392da8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfeHEtjjnfXRjEbnvw25w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VNqUJyC8e8vBVgEtDUuSzd","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Remake promo video v2","subagent_type":"fork","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Remake the Skryn promo video as a new take, v2, using the local kit in /Users/rsedykh/GitHub/skryn/promo (read promo/README.md first: storyboard, render.sh, render/*.swift, music.py, icon.py). The user asked: new icon, update the colors, and new background music. Work only inside promo/ (it's git-excluded). Don't touch docs/, the app code, git, or upload anything. Never overwrite the v1 files: write skryn-promo-v2.mp4, skryn-promo-v2-web.mp4, skryn-promo-v2-silent.mp4, skryn-promo-v2.meta.json, and a v2 poster plus stills (in a v2 subfolder, or v2-prefixed names).\n\nWhat to change:\n1. **Icon:** the title and end cards still show the old cat icon. The new icon's source is docs/assets/icon.svg (a rounded square with transparent corners, so no white knockout is needed). Render it to a 1024px transparent PNG with the cached Playwright (promo/node_modules/playwright; Chromium is fine for an SVG). Update icon.py, or replace it, so the kit no longer reads the deleted docs/icon.png.\n2. **Colors:** match the new site, which is dark only. Its tokens: paper #151517, card #1e1e21, ink #f3f2ef, muted #a3a19b, red #ff3b3b, blue #0a84ff, keycaps white (#f3f2ef, edge #8e8e93) on a dark pill (#2b2b2f). Headlines are heavy system font with tight tracking. Title and end cards go on the dark paper. Keep a per-topic background color for each chapter, but make each one a deep, muted version of its v1 tint (blue, peach, green, lavender, yellow), so the cut feels like the site rather than pastel. Captions must stay legible on them. The staged desktop and the real AnnotationView content can stay as they are. If the menu bar or keycap styling clashes, align it with the site.\n3. **End card:** icon, \"Skryn\", \"Screenshot and annotate, from the menu bar.\" (the site's line), skryn.app. **Title card:** icon, \"Skryn\", and the same line, or \"Screenshot it. Mark it up. Send it.\" (the site's headline) if that reads better. Same copy rules as v1: only claim what the app does; no \"free\", no \"open source\", no speed numbers.\n4. **Music:** write a new, fully synthesized bed (numpy/scipy via uv, like music.py) in a different style from v1's bossa. Something calm and modern that fits a dark, minimal product video, such as a soft electronic or lo-fi pulse, with tempo and phrases fitted to the cut's length and chapter times from the meta. Keep it as a separate script (e.g. music2.py) so v1 can still be rebuilt. Pick a sensible background level and report the measured integrated loudness (ffmpeg ebur128). Make sure it fades in and out cleanly, with no clicks at the joins.\n5. The app code changed since v1. Recent commits include \"Step text size along a type scale instead of ±2pt\", and build.sh patches compositeAsCGImage() in a copy of AnnotationView.swift and fails loudly if that line changed. Fix the build if needed. Keep the video's real-app behavior, and check that the ⌘= text-size steps still look right.\n\nVerify before reporting: render the full take, then look at every chapter's still and at least the title and end cards with Read. Check the duration and that audio and video are in sync. Make a contact sheet image of the stills. Also produce what the site will need when the user swaps in the new video, without touching docs/: a 1600px-wide poster.webp at q80, named so it's clearly for docs/assets/poster.webp. The poster must be a frame without the old icon. Update promo/README.md with a v2 section: what changed, the files, and how to re-render.\n\nFinal report, short: the files produced (paths), what changed in each area, measured loudness, duration, anything that didn't work or that you're unsure of, and the contact sheet path so I can show the user."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1587,"cache_read_input_tokens":564048,"output_tokens":3139,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1486},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1587,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3139,"cache_read_input_tokens":564048,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1587,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1587},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VNqUJyC8e8vBVgEtDUuSzd":{"description":"Remake promo video v2","subagent_type":"fork","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Remake the Skryn promo video as a new take, v2, using the local kit in /Users/rsedykh/GitHub/skryn/promo (read promo/README.md first: storyboard, render.sh, render/*.swift, music.py, icon.py). The user asked: new icon, update the colors, and new background music. Work only inside promo/ (it's git-excluded). Don't touch docs/, the app code, git, or upload anything. Never overwrite the v1 files: write skryn-promo-v2.mp4, skryn-promo-v2-web.mp4, skryn-promo-v2-silent.mp4, skryn-promo-v2.meta.json, and a v2 poster plus stills (in a v2 subfolder, or v2-prefixed names).\n\nWhat to change:\n1. **Icon:** the title and end cards still show the old cat icon. The new icon's source is docs/assets/icon.svg (a rounded square with transparent corners, so no white knockout is needed). Render it to a 1024px transparent PNG with the cached Playwright (promo/node_modules/playwright; Chromium is fine for an SVG). Update icon.py, or replace it, so the kit no lon