{"parentUuid":"bf3d80d1-d53a-4ec8-bfcc-d32511106844","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01JPwQEd8E9ADvpvR4364DCa","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"46dd84cf-d385-4b0a-8f1c-568d031d030a","timestamp":"2026-10-02T23:32:44.160Z","session_id":"71183914-e83d-4503-afe0-4d46d21c5038","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/rsedykh/GitHub/skryn","sessionId":"71183914-e83d-4503-afe0-4d46d21c5038","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"46dd84cf-d385-4b0a-8f1c-568d031d030a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfeHQw4RKtBPRD9R7Qj7n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the arrow. A red **\"No install needed\"** note now points at the light Try it button, with a red arrow, in the same style as the page's other marks (\"Start here\", \"Your turn\"). The note says why to click: it's true and it removes the main reason to hesitate. I went with the arrow instead of a dimmer red button because it keeps red for the marks, the way the rest of the page uses it.\n\n- **Wide windows:** the note sits above-left of the button with a diagonal arrow.\n- **Windows under 760px:** the arrow points straight down instead.\n- **Contrast:** I darkened the blur gate's overlay so the red and the white text read clearly against the pixels.\n- **Caption:** it now wraps onto two balanced lines.\n\nI checked 600, 760, 1000 and 1440px wide: nothing clipped, and the demo still works.\n\nSee it at http://127.0.0.1:8765/. Nothing is pushed yet; this change and the button restyle are local only, waiting for your go-ahead.\n\nThe video remake is running in the background:\n- the new icon on the title and end cards;\n- dark colors to match the site, with a muted tint per chapter;\n- new synthesized background music.\n\nIt saves the result as a new v2 alongside the original, and also prepares a matching poster for the site. I'll show you the stills when it's done. You'll then need to upload the new video to GitHub yourself, and I'll swap its link into the site and the README."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":693,"cache_read_input_tokens":580342,"output_tokens":464,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_t