its v1 hue as a deep tint (navy, brown, forest, indigo, olive). Captions are heavy and light; keycaps match the site's style. Captions stay legible in every chapter and during the dimmed transitions.\n- **Copy:** the title card says \"Screenshot it. Mark it up. Send it.\"; the end card says \"Screenshot and annotate, from the menu bar.\" with skryn.app.\n- **App change:** the build needed no fix. But the app now steps text size 24 → 32 → 40 and its text box is a fixed 300pt wide, so the old note wrapped onto two lines. v2 types \"Copy test key\" with one ⌘= press (to 32pt), which fits on one line. The cut is 0.42 s shorter than v1 (41.05 s vs 41.47 s).\n- **Music:** soft lo-fi electronic at 81.5 bpm, a different style from v1's bossa. A filtered pad swells under the title card, the beat starts exactly on the first chapter cut, and 12 bars build up (chord stabs, then a pluck melody with an echo, then a bell arpeggio). It resolves to a held chord exactly on the end card. No chimes on topic changes.\n- **Loudness:** −32.0 LUFS integrated, the same level as v1.\n- **Sync:** the beat measures 14 ms after its cut, the end chord 10 ms after (both under one frame), and the audio and video end together.\n- **No clicks:** I found and fixed a click at the end of every kick, a flaw v1's kick also has. The file starts and ends at exact silence, and the loudest transients all sit on the drum grid.\n- **Kit:** `TAKE=v1|v2` switches palette, icon, copy, the note and the stills folder. `render.sh` defaults to v2 and now pads the audio, so the final mux no longer drops the last 3 video frames. The `TAKE=v1` path still renders its pastel cards with the cat icon.\n\n**Unsure or not done**\n- I couldn't listen to the music. The mix balance comes from per-track levels, a spectrogram and the click scan, so it needs a real listen.\n- A v1 re-render now uses today's app, so its two ⌘= presses land on 40pt and its note wraps. It won't match `skryn-promo-v1.mp4` exactly.\n- Five screenshots (`gatearrow-*.png` and `gatebtn.png`) sit untracked in the repo root. They're not from my work; they were most likely written by the parent session's test scripts.\n- To put v2 on the site, the web encode has to be uploaded to GitHub and the URL swapped in `docs/index.html` and the README, plus the poster replaced. The steps are in the promo README.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>673816</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>46</tool_uses><duration_ms>748072</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"c8bdbb76-c476-4911-9e18-582bce9fc59e","timestamp":"2026-10-02T23:43:27.099Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":27,"turnIndex":32},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/rsedykh/GitHub/skryn","sessionId":"71183914-e83d-4503-afe0-4d46d21c5038","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"main"}
