{"parentUuid":"802fd14b-1c86-4cb3-b3a7-f473c159d155","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f6b3c9d9-1083-42cb-b539-75c1c741592f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>adfde5ca4fa51246c</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01BKGSPp3ciiCSSRnfinptp5</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>REDACTED.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Remake promo video v2\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>v3 is rendered: plum and teal chapters replace the brown and gold, and the music is a new chill techno track. I looked at every chapter still, the caption dims and the poster. v1 and v2 files are untouched, and nothing was written outside `promo/`.\n\n**Files**\n- `skryn-promo-v3.mp4`, `-web.mp4` (4.3 MB), `-silent.mp4` and `.meta.json`.\n- `stills/v3/`.\n- `skryn-promo-v3-contact-sheet.png`.\n- `poster-v3.jpg` (30.5 s, the crop, no old icon).\n- `v3-for-docs/assets/poster.webp` (1600 px, q80).\n- New `music3.py`. Edited `render/Stage.swift`, `render/main.swift`, `render.sh` and `README.md`, which has a v3 section. `TAKE` now accepts `v1|v2|v3` and defaults to v3.\n\n**Chapter colors** (deep base / glow / highlight)\n- Capture: navy `#121b29` / `#1f3a63` / `#182436` (as v2).\n- Tools: **plum** `#1d1022` / `#56245a` / `#281631` (was brown).\n- Marks: forest `#111c15` / `#21462c` / `#16251b` (as v2).\n- Edit: indigo `#18152a` / `#3b2f6b` / `#1f1b33` (as v2).\n- Output: **deep teal** `#0c1c1f` / `#1a525a` / `#12282c` (was olive/gold).\n- Title and end cards stay on the site's `#151517`.\n\nEach chapter is distinct from its neighbors, and captions and keycaps are legible on all of them.\n\n**Music:** chill deep minimal techno, 122.2 bpm, A minor, 18 bars.\n- **Title card:** a filtered Am9 pad swells, one dub stab echoes, and a soft riser leads in.\n- **Drop:** a soft, rounded four-on-the-floor kick starts on the first chapter cut, with offbeat hats and a rolling filtered bassline. Over it, dub chord stabs (Am9/Fmaj9) go through a dotted-eighth ping-pong delay with a light sidechain pump.\n- **Build:** 16 bars add layers every four: the bass fills in, then shakers, soft claps on 2 and 4, and the stab filter opens.\n- **Lift:** two bars of filter sweep and a riser on G6/9. The kick drops for the last two beats.\n- **End card:** an Am9 stab and one last kick land on it, then the echoes ring out.\n\n**Measurements**\n- **Loudness:** −32.1 LUFS integrated, LRA 2.4 LU.\n- **Sync:** the drop lands 8 ms after its cut and the end chord 11 ms after (both under one frame).\n- **Clean edges and no stray clicks:** the first and last samples are exactly silent, and every loud high-frequency burst sits on the 16th grid (hats and shakers).\n- **Duration:** 41.05 s, all 2463 frames, with audio and video ending together.\n\n**Unsure**\n- I couldn't listen to the music. The balance comes from per-track levels, a spectrogram and peak checks, so it needs a real listen.\n- The kick fundamental (~44 Hz) won't come through laptop speakers. The pulse should still read through the bass harmonics, hats and stab pump, but that's unverified.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>647048</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>18</tool_uses><duration_ms>504553</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"373c3da2-a64f-4ec9-a005-84d1cf0d15fc","timestamp":"2026-10-02T23:56:56.293Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":33,"turnIndex":39},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/rsedykh/GitHub/skryn","sessionId":"71183914-e83d-4503-afe0-4d46d21c5038","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"main"}
